From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:36:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Fix first compileJava error batch: MelonBlock removal,
 Blueprint/Neapolitan/Spirit deps

- Vanilla's MelonBlock class was removed in 1.21 (Blocks.MELON is now a plain Block); MiniBlock
  and SlicedMiniMelonBlock now extend Block directly instead of the nonexistent MelonBlock.
- Deleted DelightfulCauldronInteractions.java and SpiritCompat.java: both compiled against real
  third-party APIs (com.teamabnormals.blueprint / com.teamabnormals.neapolitan,
  me.codexadrian.spirit) that were compileOnly/implementation dependencies in the old 1.20.1
  Forge build.gradle but are not declared (and not in the target pack) for this NeoForge port.
  Both were already dead code without their mods present (gated by Modid.N.loaded() /
  Modid.SP-based enabled() checks), so stripped them the same way as the Botania/Aether/
  LetFishLove compat: DelightfulBlocks' milkshake cauldrons now always use a plain empty
  CauldronInteraction map, ModEvents drops the registerCauldronInteractions() call, and
  SoulSteelKnifeItem drops the SpiritCompat hurtEnemy/tooltip hooks (it's already
  Spirit-gated via getModid() so this was unreachable regardless).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
